Team 13, Milestone 02: Forward position kinematics (EDPT-1009, Winter 2026)

REPORT
- Team13_Milestone02_Report.docx   the report (Word), building on the Milestone 01 report
- Team13_Milestone02_Report.pdf    the same report as PDF
- Report_LaTeX_source.zip          LaTeX source and figures of the report

SCRIPTS (run everything from inside this folder)
MATLAB functions
- transformation_func.m            T = transformation_func(theta, d, a, alpha): DH matrix of one row (symbolic angle)
- forward_kinematics_func.m        X = forward_kinematics_func(): multiplies the 4 DH matrices, returns symbolic [x; y; z]
- print_fk_equations.m             prints x, y, z and 0T4, and evaluates test cases A and B
- test_transformation_func_RR.m    checks transformation_func against Tutorial 03, Example 1
- plot_dh_frames.m                 draws the DH frames at q = [0 0 0 0]
Simulink / Simscape Multibody
- robot_fk_test.slx                test model: q_deg (degrees, base workspace) drives the arm; displays the
                                   Simscape end effector, the forward-kinematics end effector and their error.
                                   Set q_deg (default [30 20 -40 25]) and press Run; Mechanics Explorer opens.
- run_fk_tests.m                   simulates test cases A and B and prints Simscape vs forward kinematics
- robot_matlab.slx                 the arm imported from robot_matlab.urdf with smimport
- build_fk_test_model.m            builds robot_fk_test.slx from robot_matlab.slx
- robot_matlab.urdf, meshes/       the course URDF and meshes used for the import
Python (ROS 2 Jazzy)
- forward_kinematics.py            transformation_func and forward_kinematics_func with SymPy
- fk_gazebo_node.py                ROS 2 node: publishes the joint angles on /Joint_1..4/command and subscribes to
                                   /end_effector_pose in Gazebo, then prints Gazebo vs forward kinematics.
                                   Usage, with the course package's spawn_gazebo.launch.py running:
                                   python3 fk_gazebo_node.py 30 20 -40 25   (angles in degrees)

No XML file is included: no CAD modifications were made in this milestone, and the Simscape model is
imported from the course URDF.

RESULTS (end effector, world frame)
- Case A, q = (0, 0, 0, 0):          Simscape and Gazebo agree with the equations to within 0.026 mm
- Case B, q = (30, 20, -40, 25) deg: Simscape and Gazebo agree with the equations to within 0.027 mm

MEDIA
- Video1.mp4   MATLAB functions and Simscape Multibody simulation (captioned)
- Video2.mp4   Gazebo simulation and the Python ROS 2 node (captioned)
